  "description": "Sprengisandsleið, road F26: 154 km across Iceland's central highlands, ranging between about 250 and 830 m. Almost the whole length is gravel; OpenStreetMap tags it as four-wheel-drive only and records a ford on the route. Camp and hut sites at Nýidalur and Versalir are mapped within 150 m of the track; plan fuel and supplies before you set out. Highland F-roads are mountain tracks, not ordinary roads.\n\nRoute data © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL). OSM ways with ref F26 (22 ways; ids in Nomad sources file).\nCover photo: Andreas Tille / CC BY-SA 4.0 / Wikimedia Commons.",
